# Block32 goal

Classify whether the first complete guarded transaction built from Blocks
28--31 selects the returned-pair law parameter, and at the same time replace
Block31's token-to-route correspondence by an exact factor-level controlled
successor channel.

For the four exits lateral to a returned front, retain the full family

\[
 q_\lambda(g,h)=
 \begin{cases}
 (1+3\lambda)/16,&g=h,\\
 (1-\lambda)/16,&g\ne h,
 \end{cases}
 \qquad 0\leq\lambda<1.
\]

Let `U` be the frozen Block31 nearest-neighbor ordered-pair transducer.  After
`U`, each exact complete Block28 pointer configuration must select one of
sixteen orthogonal token sectors.  In that sector the target runner must
construct the direct-sum channel

\[
 L_{r,\alpha}=U^\dagger W_r R_{r,\alpha}P_rU,
 \qquad
 L_{\rm STOP}=U^\dagger(I-P_A)U,
 \qquad P_A=\sum_rP_r.
\]

Here `P_r` includes the complete input pointer word, the one-hot token, clean
transient comparator cells, a Blank persistent selector, and the declared
Block30 Blank carrier; `R_{r,alpha}` is the literal ten-step handoff followed
by the reached second pair instrument; and `W_r` writes one persistent
one-hot route selector.  The runner must prove exact CP/TP, complement STOP,
old-Record QND action, `U`/`U^dagger` cleanup, no-refire from selector and
Blank debit, the complete resource update, proper-cubic/side covariance, and
the two-use prefix identity symbolically in `lambda`.

The decisive output is the exact subset of `[0,1)` surviving all those
constraints.  A discrete subset is a process-law selector.  Survival of the
whole interval is a narrowly scoped nonselection result for this transaction,
not a universal no-go.  An empty subset localizes a contradiction in the
named composition.  Timeout or incomplete execution carries no inference.

This block is at the repository's literal local-Kraus-factor standard.  It
does not compile the complete 26-bit pointer projector, the local writer
Stinespring rotations, or the full transaction into one nearest-neighbor gate
